"screentime.configured" = "Screen Time adult-content filter configured";
"screentime.notConfigured" = "Screen Time filter not confirmed";
"screentime.enable" = "Enable personal Screen Time protection";
"screentime.disable" = "Turn off Hisn's Screen Time filter";
"screentime.scope" = "Apple's automatic adult-content web filter is an additional layer, not a guarantee for all apps or images. Personal authorization can be revoked in system settings and does not prevent deletion. Hisn reads configuration, not real-world blocking success. The filter remains configured after the plan ends until you choose to turn it off.";
"screentime.consentTitle" = "Add Screen Time for self-control?";
"screentime.consentBody" = "Authorize your own account with Apple, without a partner. Hisn will configure Apple's automatic adult-content web filter. Existing authorized access is reused, not replaced with weaker self-authorization. No uninstall lock is promised. During your commitment Hisn will not offer to disable this filter.";
"screentime.failed" = "Screen Time authorization or configuration could not be confirmed. Check Apple's permission and the Family Controls entitlement. Your other protection layers and commitment are unchanged.";
"screentime.simulator" = "Personal Screen Time protection needs a signed, entitled build on your real device. Simulator cannot verify this protection. Your commitment is unchanged.";
"removal.title" = "Optional family removal protection";
"network.title" = "An independent home-network layer";
"network.steps" = "If you own or administer your router, use its official guide to set adult-content filtering DNS for the home network: 1.1.1.3 and 1.0.0.3, including the provider's IPv6 settings where supported. Keep a record of the previous settings. Then check from each device. No router password is collected by Hisn.";
"network.scope" = "This manual router layer survives closing Hisn, but only protects traffic that uses that network and DNS. Mobile data, alternate DNS and VPNs may bypass it. Hisn does not upload lists or change the router automatically here, and cannot confirm this layer from the phone. Keep recovery available; do not erase router credentials.";
"network.guide" = "Cloudflare's official router setup guide";
"removal.notRequested" = "Guardian authorization not requested";
"removal.denied" = "Authorization denied or revoked";
"removal.scopeUnknown" = "Approved access; child authorization not verified";
"removal.accepted" = "Child request accepted — verify on device";
"removal.unavailable" = "Unavailable here; a real child device is required";
"removal.body" = "On a child's device, Apple's guardian-approved Family Controls authorization prevents removal of this parental-control app while authorization remains active. Self-authorization does not prevent deletion. This does not lock DNS or Safari settings.";
"removal.request" = "Request guardian authorization";
"removal.consent.title" = "Authorize protection on a child's device?";
"removal.consent.body" = "A parent or guardian in the same Apple Family Sharing group must approve Apple's prompt on the child's device. Active child authorization prevents removal of Hisn and iCloud sign-out. Only continue with the guardian present and consenting. No weaker self-authorization will be requested if this fails.";
"removal.manual" = "For self-use, ask a trusted person to configure Screen Time's app-deletion restriction and keep its separate passcode. On iOS 16–26, look under Content & Privacy Restrictions → iTunes & App Store Purchases (or App Installations & Purchases) → Deleting Apps → Don't Allow. Newer layouts vary; use Apple's guide. Hisn cannot verify this manual restriction.";
"removal.recovery" = "The guardian retains control and can revoke Screen Time access through Apple's settings. After restarting Hisn, an approved status alone cannot prove child authorization; verify with the guardian. Removing the Home Screen icon is not the same as uninstalling. Device reset and guardian revocation are not prevented.";
"removal.guide" = "Apple's family setup guide";
"removal.simulator" = "Guardian authorization cannot be tested in Simulator. Use a signed build on a real child's device with a guardian in the same family.";
"removal.failed" = "Child authorization was not confirmed. Check the child account, Family Sharing, guardian approval and the app's Family Controls entitlement. No fallback authorization was requested.";
"family.steps" = "Add Screen Time's adult-website restriction in Content & Privacy Restrictions. For family protection, let a trusted guardian keep its passcode.";
"family.scope" = "Hisn can configure its own app shields and adult-web filter after Apple authorization. The family Screen Time settings described here are manual and unverified; managed-device enforcement is not included.";
"language.title" = "Language";
"language.system" = "Follow device language";
"privacy.title" = "Privacy";
"privacy.body" = "Hisn does not record visited sites or blocked browsing attempts. Safari applies declarative rules without sending browsing history to Hisn. Family DNS is handled by Cloudflare under its own privacy policy.";
"coverage.title" = "What this version protects";
"coverage.body" = "A self-control commitment, Safari domain blocking, optional family DNS and Apple's adult-content web filter. This does not guarantee all content, all apps, VPN resistance or protection that cannot be disabled. It works independently of your Mac; settings do not sync yet.";
"apple.title" = "iPhone and iPad";
"apple.body" = "One universal app for iOS and iPadOS 16 or later. Real-device DNS and Screen Time need signing and matching DNS Settings and Family Controls capabilities. Family Controls distribution also requires Apple's entitlement approval. An unsigned build is not an installable phone release.";
